    {
      "label": "Description",
      "value": "Flap figure: Large woodcut colored anatomical figures of a man and a skeleton; the man having three moveable flaps and a fourth base layer. Flap one depicts the torso, flap two depicts several internal organs, such as the intestines, lungs, liver, stomach, flap three depicts the bladder, kidneys, urinary and seminal system. The final flap (base layer) depicts the skeletal system. 4 unnumbered leaves : color illustrations"
    },
